# Template for a parallel, non-disruptive test environment used during
# steps 1-7 of the native migration, BEFORE the actual cutover.
#
# On the EC2 host, copy the real .env.production and override just the
# lines below (do not create this from scratch - reuse the real DB
# credentials, Dhan credentials, SMTP settings, etc. from .env.production):
#
#   cp /opt/option-decode/repo/.env.production /opt/option-decode/shared/.env.native-test
#   # then edit the overrides below into it
#
# Why overrides are needed at all (rather than just reusing
# .env.production as-is) and what's actually safe to run in parallel:
#
# - WEB_PORT / API_PORT are bumped to 3001/4001 so the native web/api can
#   run alongside the still-live Docker stack (which owns 3000/4000
#   inside its network and 80/443 via nginx) without a port collision.
#
# - REDIS_URL points at the native redis-server's default port (6379).
#   This is naturally isolated from Docker's redis, since the Docker
#   redis service has no `ports:` mapping in docker-compose.prod.yml -
#   it's only reachable inside the Docker network by container DNS name,
#   never from the host. No conflict, no shared queue.
#
# - DATABASE_URL still points at the SAME production MySQL (native, only
#   one instance exists). That's fine for web/api - they're predominantly
#   serving requests, same risk profile as the real thing. It is NOT
#   fine to leave the WORKER running for an extended period against this
#   same database with the same DHAN credentials while the Docker worker
#   is also running - you'd get two workers polling/writing the same
#   capture jobs, duplicate rows, doubled alerts, and two WebSocket
#   clients authenticating with the same Dhan credentials. Use the
#   worker unit only for short verification bursts (confirm it starts,
#   connects to DB/Redis/Dhan cleanly, logs look right) and then
#   `systemctl stop option-decode-worker` again - don't leave it running
#   until the actual cutover.

WEB_PORT=3001
API_PORT=4001
REDIS_URL=redis://127.0.0.1:6379/0

# Everything else (DATABASE_URL, DHAN_*, SESSION_SECRET, JWT_SECRET, SMTP_*)
# stays as-is from the real .env.production.
